---
title: Updating your project
sidebar:
  order: 5
---

In VS Code, open a terminal (**Terminal > New Terminal**), then:

## Add papermario-dx as a remote named `upstream`

```sh
git remote add upstream https://github.com/bates64/papermario-dx.git
```

## Fetch the latest changes

```sh
git fetch upstream --tags --force
```

## Merge the version you want into your `main` branch

Paper Mario DX marks releases with tags, such as `dx-nightly` for the latest development build:

```sh
git checkout main
git merge upstream/dx-nightly
```

Replace `dx-nightly` with a specific version tag (for example `dx-1.0`) for a stable release instead.

## Resolve any merge conflicts

VS Code highlights conflicting sections in the editor with buttons like **Accept Current Change**, **Accept Incoming Change**, and **Accept Both Changes**. Stage each resolved file in the Source Control panel (**Ctrl+Shift+G**), then commit the merge.

## Build

Build as usual with **Ctrl+Shift+B**.
